  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q = \\Delta U + W\"></span> [1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W = Q_{in} - Q_{out} = 2500 - 1500 = 1000\\ \\text{J}\"></span><br/>[1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong></p><p>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta = \\frac{W}{Q_{in}} = \\frac{1000}{2500}\"></span><br/>[1 mark]<br/>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta = 0.40 = 40\\%\"></span><br/>[1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong></p><p>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta_{\\text{Carnot}} = 1 - \\frac{T_C}{T_H} = 1 - \\frac{300}{600}\"></span><br/>[1 mark]<br/>- <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta_{\\text{Carnot}} = 0.50 = 50\\%\"></span><br/>[1 mark]</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"e\"><p><strong>e</strong></p><p>No; the actual efficiency (40%) is less than the Carnot limit (50%), so the engine is not reversible.<br/>[1 mark]</p></section>"
