  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A heat engine absorbs <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2500\\ \\text{J}\"></span> of thermal energy from a hot reservoir at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"600\\ \\text{K}\"></span>, and rejects <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1500\\ \\text{J}\"></span> of thermal energy to a cold reservoir at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"300\\ \\text{K}\"></span>.</p><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> </p>State the first law of thermodynamics.<p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p>Determine the work output of the engine per cycle.<p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> </p>Calculate the efficiency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta\"></span> of this heat engine.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> </p>Calculate the maximum possible efficiency for a heat engine operating between these two temperatures.<p>[2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"e\"><p><strong>e</strong> </p>Comment on whether this engine is reversible.<p>[1]</p></section>"
